      <p>For information on boot image management, see "Boot image management".</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: MachineConfiguration\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\nstatus:\n# ...\n  bootImageSkewEnforcementStatus:\n    automatic:\n      ocpVersion: 4.22.0\n    mode: Automatic"} lang="yaml" title="Example MachineConfiguration object with automatic skew enforcement" />
      <p>The MCO examines the boot image reported in the <code>ocpVersion</code> parameter to determine if the cluster is violating the boot image version skew limits.</p>
      </dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Manual</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>When set to <code>Manual</code>, if the boot image version is updated, a cluster administrator is responsible for manually updating the <code>MachineConfiguration</code> object with the RHCOS version of the new boot image or the OpenShift Container Platform version associated with the new boot image. The MCO then tests the boot image version for skew.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: MachineConfiguration\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\n# ...\nspec:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcement:\n    mode: Manual\n    manual:\n      mode: RHCOSVersion\n      rhcosVersion: 9.2.20251023-0\n# ...\nstatus:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcementStatus:\n    manual:\n      mode: RHCOSVersion\n      rhcosVersion: 9.2.20251023-0\n    mode: Manual"} lang="yaml" title="Example MachineConfiguration object with skew enforcement based on an RHCOS version" />
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: MachineConfiguration\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\n# ...\nspec:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcement:\n    manual:\n      mode: OCPVersion\n      ocpVersion: 4.22.0\n    mode: Manual\n# ...\nstatus:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcementStatus:\n    manual:\n      mode: OCPVersion\n      ocpVersion: 4.22.0\n    mode: Manual"} lang="yaml" title="Example MachineConfiguration object with skew enforcement based on an OpenShift Container Platform version" />
      <p>The MCO examines the boot image reported in the <code>rhcosVersion</code> or <code>ocpVersion</code> parameter to determine if the cluster is violating the boot image version skew limits.</p>
      </dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">None</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>When set to <code>None</code>, boot image skew enforcement is disabled. When disabled, the MCO does not monitor for boot image skew and does not report if new nodes are provisioned with older boot images, which could introduce issues when scaling new nodes.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: MachineConfiguration\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\n# ...\nspec:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcement:\n    mode: None\n# ...\nstatus:\n  bootImageSkewEnforcementStatus:\n    mode: None"} lang="yaml" title="Example MachineConfiguration object with skew enforcement disabled" />
      <p>When in the none mode, the MCO reports a Prometheus alert that skew enforcement is disabled and that scale-up might run into issues due to old boot images. The alert does not cause any functional issues for the cluster.</p>
